# i18n Sync

When adding or changing **user-facing text** (labels, titles, toasts, dialogs, errors shown in UI), sync translations in the same change.

## Project convention

- UI code uses `'English source string'.tr` (see `lib/core/localization/app_locale.dart`).
- **Key** = the exact English string passed to `.tr`.
- Maps live in `lib/i18n/en_US.dart` and `lib/i18n/zh_CN.dart`; both must define every key used in code.

## Required workflow

1. **Add or update the key in both maps** — never only one locale file.
2. **Use the same key string** in Dart and in both maps (character-for-character).
3. **Prefer English keys in stores** for errors/messages; call `.tr` when displaying (e.g. `error.tr` in widgets).
4. **Do not hardcode** user-visible Chinese or English in widgets/stores — use `.tr` unless the value is not shown to users (logs, debug).

## Examples

```dart
// ✅ GOOD — key in both i18n files
title: Text('Export History'.tr),

// ❌ BAD — missing from lib/i18n/*.dart
title: const Text('Export History'),

// ✅ GOOD — store holds key; UI translates
errorMessage.value = 'Model file not found';
// in widget: Text(error.tr)
```

```dart
// lib/i18n/en_US.dart
'Local file': 'Local file',

// lib/i18n/zh_CN.dart
'Local file': '本地文件',
```

## Before marking work complete

- [ ] Grep for new/changed `.tr` keys and confirm entries exist in **both** `en_US` and `zh_CN`.
- [ ] No orphaned keys removed from code but left only in one locale (clean up unused keys when safe).
- [ ] For ambiguous or easily confused strings, add a check in `test/i18n/` if the project already tests similar copy.

## Out of scope

- Comments, commit messages, ADR/docs (English unless user asks otherwise).
- Third-party / plugin UI we do not control.
